{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"\"This is bad - drop this branch and start over from master.\" Guarded destructive workflow. A dirty tree or a merge in flight is REFUSED unless discard=true, which runs merge --abort / reset --hard HEAD / clean -fd so no edit and no new store record survives. Then checkout the default branch (master, else main) -> branch -D <branch> -> (delete_remote=true) push origin --delete <branch>; origin's copy is KEPT by default, so an abandon is recoverable from the remote -> when next_branch is non-empty, dev.git.start_branch takes over (fetch, fast-forward default to origin, cut, publish) and the result rides under `next`; otherwise the default branch is fetched and fast-forwarded to origin's in place. Refuses the default branch itself or a nonexistent branch; the mutating-command confirm gate is the 'are you sure?' by mechanism. Returns {status, msg, abandoned, now_on, discarded, remote_deleted, next, steps}.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"branch","type":"String"},{"name":"discard","type":"Boolean"},{"name":"delete_remote","type":"Boolean"},{"name":"next_branch","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"hgoiwu1a05cfe25f6g11c","readers":[],"time":1788639902193,"username":"system","writers":[]}